    "title": "Duke women's basketball unseats LSU in NCAA Women's Sweet 16",
    "text": "March 27, 2026Updated March 28, 2026, 12:34 a.m. ETNo. 3-seeded Duke women's basketball (26-8) survived and advanced from the Sweet 16 of the NCAA Women's Tournament, unleashing revenge on another, this time a juggernaut, 87-85, against LSU on March 27.Duke got out to a hot start and kept it rolling the entire game. Senior guard Ashlon Jackson hit a 3-pointer at the buzzer to take the victory, finishing with 19 points, 2 rebounds and 5 assists.LSU managed to catch up and take the lead briefly, making it a neck-and-neck battle for the two hungry squads, but a steal and failed layup by Mi'Laysia Fulwiley off a turnover by Toby Fournier kept Duke in the game.See what happened between No. 3 Duke-No. 2 LSU women's basketball in the Sweet 16 of the NCAA Women's Tournament:Buy Duke women's basketball ticketsDuke vs LSU women's basketball live updatesTEAM1Q2Q3Q4QFINALDuke2423202087LSU1921252085 12:24 a.m. | Duke punches Elite Eight ticket thanks to senior guardThe Blue Devils defeated the Lady Tigers 87-85 in the Sweet 16, punching back-to-back Elite Eight appearances with a massive upset. Taina Mair and Toby Fournier had 22 points apiece and Ashlon Jackson, who hit the buzzer-beating 3-point basket, finished with 19 points. 11:39 p.m. | LSU-Duke locked in back-and-forth battle as third quarter endsThe Blue Devils lead the Lady Tigers 67-65 at the end of the third quarter. Taina Mair has 19 points, Toby Fournier 18 points and Ashlon Jackson 11 points to lead Duke. Arianna Roberson adds 9 points and 10 rebounds.LSU managed to catch up in this quarter, outscoring Duke 25-20. 11:06 p.m. | LSU unable to catch up to Duke in first halfThe Blue Devils lead the Lady Tigers 47-40 at the half. Arianna Roberson is near a double-double with 9 points, 9 rebounds, while Toby Fournier leads with 14 points. 10:36 p.m. | Duke leads LSU at the end of the first quarterThe Blue Devils lead the Lady Tigers 24-19 at the end of the first quarter. Arianna Roberson has 9 points, 3 rebounds, 1 block and 1 steal. Toby Fournier has 6 points, 3 rebounds and 1 steal.LSU has not held the lead since the score was 2-0 in the first 15 seconds. Mi'Laysia Fulwiley has 10 points on perfect shooting. Duke vs LSU women's basketball startersDuke: Ashlon Jackson, Riley Nelson, Delaney Thomas, Taina Mair, Toby Fournier.LSU: Flau'jae Johnson, ZaKiyah Johnson, Mikaylah Williams, Kate Koval, Jada Richard.What channel is Duke vs LSU women's basketball on today?TV channel: ESPNStreaming: ESPN Unlimited, FuboDuke vs. LSU women's basketball is being broadcast on ESPN and will be available for streaming via ESPN Unlimited or Fubo, which offers a free trial for new subscribers.Duke vs LSU women's basketball time todayDate: Friday, March 27Time: 10 p.m. ETDuke vs. LSU women's basketball tips off at 10 p.m. ET from Golden 1 Center in Sacramento, Calif., on Friday, March 27.Duke vs LSU women's basketball historySeries record: Tied, 3-3Duke's last win: March 22, 2010; 60-52 (NCAA Tournament)LSU's last win: Dec. 4, 2025; 93-77Duke women's basketball schedule 2025-26Record: 26-8 overall, 16-2 ACCNovember (3-5)Nov. 3: Baylor 58, Duke 52Nov. 9: Duke 91, Holy Cross 48Nov. 12: Duke 83, Norfolk State 32Nov. 14: West Virginia 57, Duke 49Nov. 16: Duke 71, Liberty 57Nov. 20: South Florida 85, Duke 72Nov. 26: South Carolina 83, Duke 66Nov. 27: UCLA 89, Duke 59December (4-1)Dec. 4: LSU 93, Duke 77Dec. 7: Duke 70, Virginia Tech 54Dec. 18: Duke 97, South Dakota State 54Dec. 20: Duke 76, Belmont 46Dec. 28: Duke 71, Syracuse 51January (8-0)Jan. 1: Duke 100, Boston College 49Jan. 4: Duke 82, Notre Dame 68Jan. 8: Duke 78, Cal 74Jan. 11: Duke 67, Stanford 60Jan. 15: Duke 65, Virginia 58Jan. 18: Duke 93, Georgia Tech 46Jan. 24: Duke 95, Pitt 41Jan. 29: Duke 74, Miami 58February (6-1)Feb. 1: Duke 80, Wake Forest 44Feb. 5: Duke 59, Louisville 58Feb. 8: Duke 95, SMU 36Feb. 15: Duke 72, UNC 68Feb. 19: Duke 83, NC State 65Feb. 22: Clemson 53, Duke 51Feb. 26: Duke 80, Florida State 52March (5-1)March 1: UNC 74, Duke 69March 6: Duke 60, Clemson 46March 7: Duke 65, Notre Dame 63March 8: Duke 70, Louisville 65 (OT)March 20: Duke 81, Charleston 64March 22: Duke 69, Baylor 46March 27: vs. LSU, 10 p.m. (ESPN)March 30-31: NCAA Women's Elite EightAprilApril 3: NCAA Women's Final Four — Phoenix, Ariz.April 5: NCAA Women's Championship — Phoenix, Ariz.",
